1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:03,970
Training gives you a place to publish
instructions, assign people, and

2
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:05,699
review their recorded progress.

3
00:00:06,090 --> 00:00:09,869
We are on the New Training form in
the fictional Chicago Fire department.

4
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:15,119
Enter Academy, Shared contact verification
exercise as the Training name.

5
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:19,170
Use Description for a short explanation
of what the training is about.

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,590
Here it says that this is
practice finding and checking

7
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:24,639
fictional operational contacts.

8
00:00:24,979 --> 00:00:28,620
A clear title and description help
a member recognize the assignment

9
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:30,360
before opening the full lesson.

10
00:00:30,619 --> 00:00:34,250
Training Text is the separate area
for the instructions themselves.

11
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:39,099
Our exercise asks the learner to
open Contacts, find Academy Partner

12
00:00:39,099 --> 00:00:43,280
Directory, check the contact
identity and current details, and

13
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:45,120
reopen an entry after an edit.

14
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:48,010
Read the complete paragraph
before assigning it.

15
00:00:48,449 --> 00:00:52,000
It gives someone a concrete task
and a way to verify the result.

16
00:00:52,359 --> 00:00:56,900
The wording also makes clear that the
exercise does not authorize real outreach.

17
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:00,100
Keep the catalog description
short and put the actual

18
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:01,799
learning steps in Training Text.

19
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:05,990
Set Minimum Score to one hundred
percent for this one-question exercise

20
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:09,869
and choose November fifteenth,
twenty twenty-six as its Due Date.

21
00:01:10,329 --> 00:01:12,789
Review the audience before
creating the training.

22
00:01:13,190 --> 00:01:17,520
Add all Personnel is checked here, which
selects the whole fictional department.

23
00:01:17,989 --> 00:01:22,690
Groups To Add, Roles To Add, and Users
To Add are the narrower alternatives

24
00:01:22,719 --> 00:01:24,430
when you choose a smaller audience.

25
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:28,700
Do not assume a previously selected
individual limits an assignment

26
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:30,809
while Add all Personnel is checked.

27
00:01:31,180 --> 00:01:34,500
We will verify the resulting
fourteen assignments after saving.

28
00:01:34,790 --> 00:01:39,209
In Questions, use Add Question
and enter: What should you do

29
00:01:39,209 --> 00:01:41,149
after updating a shared contact?

30
00:01:41,509 --> 00:01:42,759
Add two answers.

31
00:01:43,110 --> 00:01:47,770
The first says to reopen the saved
contact and verify the updated details.

32
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:51,410
The second says to assume the
edit was saved without checking.

33
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:55,070
Mark the first answer as
correct using its radio control.

34
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:59,519
Check the question, both answers,
and the selected correct answer

35
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:01,310
before choosing Add Training.

36
00:02:01,769 --> 00:02:04,830
One clear question is enough
to demonstrate the difference

37
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:08,060
between assigning content and
checking the learner’s response.

38
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:11,930
The new training appears in the catalog
with its description and due date,

39
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,359
alongside the existing training entries.

40
00:02:14,819 --> 00:02:18,080
Open Report for this training
before completing the exercise.

41
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:22,649
The report separates Viewed,
Completed, Score, and Result.

42
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:28,479
Boden’s initial row says Not Viewed,
Not Completed, No Score, and Pending.

43
00:02:28,910 --> 00:02:33,309
An assignment has been created, but that
row does not yet record participation.

44
00:02:33,690 --> 00:02:36,850
Use these separate columns to
decide whether someone has opened

45
00:02:36,850 --> 00:02:40,469
the training, submitted the
quiz, or met the required score.

46
00:02:40,639 --> 00:02:43,069
Open View Training for the saved exercise.

47
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:46,909
Check the title, due date,
description, and full training

48
00:02:46,909 --> 00:02:48,369
text from the learner’s side.

49
00:02:48,770 --> 00:02:52,289
This training has a quiz, so
opening its page records that it

50
00:02:52,289 --> 00:02:55,959
was viewed; the learner still needs
to answer and submit the quiz.

51
00:02:56,459 --> 00:02:59,410
Take Quiz is a separate action
in the right-hand panel.

52
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:03,490
Before taking it, review the
instructions and any training files.

53
00:03:03,879 --> 00:03:07,359
The learner view is a useful check
that the content people receive

54
00:03:07,359 --> 00:03:09,029
matches what you meant to assign.

55
00:03:09,229 --> 00:03:12,110
Choose Take Quiz and
read the welcome stage.

56
00:03:12,430 --> 00:03:14,609
Use Next to open Question One.

57
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:18,120
The same question and two
answers from the training editor

58
00:03:18,170 --> 00:03:19,950
now appear as learner choices.

59
00:03:20,319 --> 00:03:23,769
Select the answer that says to
reopen the saved contact and

60
00:03:23,769 --> 00:03:25,589
verify the updated details.

61
00:03:25,939 --> 00:03:28,599
The filled radio control
shows the current choice.

62
00:03:28,970 --> 00:03:30,300
Use Next to continue.

63
00:03:30,769 --> 00:03:34,359
Selecting an answer is still
preparation; a quiz result is

64
00:03:34,359 --> 00:03:36,300
recorded after the learner submits it.

65
00:03:36,689 --> 00:03:39,870
You can use Previous to review
the question before finishing.

66
00:03:40,139 --> 00:03:43,919
At the Finish stage, read the
instruction to submit the quiz answers.

67
00:03:44,290 --> 00:03:48,260
The Finish control at the lower right
performs that submission; the Finish

68
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:50,930
label across the top identifies the stage.

69
00:03:51,309 --> 00:03:53,750
Submit once and check
the returned catalog.

70
00:03:54,170 --> 00:03:57,719
For Boden, this exercise
now shows Training Complete.

71
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:00,729
That is the completion indicator
for the current learner.

72
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:04,680
Open Report to check the score and
pass result as well, rather than

73
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:07,920
treating a completed submission
as proof of the required score.

74
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:12,520
An administrator can add another handout
after a learner has completed the quiz.

75
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:16,189
This training already lists the
original contact-verification

76
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:18,390
file and quick-check dot txt.

77
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:23,830
On Edit, Existing Attachments identifies
those saved files and Currently

78
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:26,270
Assigned still shows fourteen users.

79
00:04:26,649 --> 00:04:29,930
Under Add Attachments,
choose review dot txt.

80
00:04:30,409 --> 00:04:34,739
Check the selected filename and use Save
Training at the bottom of this form.

81
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:39,620
Reopen the learner view: Training
files now lists all three handouts.

82
00:04:39,930 --> 00:04:42,879
This completed learner has
no Take Quiz panel here.

83
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:46,309
Verify the assignment count
and existing result separately

84
00:04:46,339 --> 00:04:47,550
when maintaining a training.

85
00:04:47,830 --> 00:04:51,519
After that edit, Report still
shows Boden’s completed quiz,

86
00:04:51,690 --> 00:04:53,720
score of one hundred, and Pass.

87
00:04:54,169 --> 00:04:57,829
Viewed records the most recent
opening, so its displayed time can

88
00:04:57,829 --> 00:04:59,539
be later than the completion time.

89
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:02,159
The other thirteen
assignments remain Pending.

90
00:05:02,579 --> 00:05:04,430
Follow up with those learners separately.

91
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:08,809
Chicago Fire can use this workflow
for a department software refresher.

92
00:05:09,210 --> 00:05:12,960
Community care and mental health
teams can assign operational process

93
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:17,800
learning; search and rescue can review
support procedures; security teams can

94
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:22,219
teach site workflows; wildland crews
can prepare seasonal information;

95
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:26,359
and industrial response teams can
review facility coordination steps.

96
00:05:26,809 --> 00:05:29,800
These recorded results describe
this training and quiz;

97
00:05:30,129 --> 00:05:33,539
professional qualifications belong
in their own reviewed process.

